 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, use the line shown to identify and draw the union or intersection of sets.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/6e08a5970c41c115.png\" alt=\"A line with three points, A, B, and C marked on it.\">\n</figure>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532716,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"{\\overline {AB}}  \\cap {\\overline {BC}}\">{\\overline {AB}}  \\cap {\\overline {BC}}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You are looking for the intersection of line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {AB} \"></span> and line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {BC} \"></span>.</p>\n<p>Sketch the two line segments separately above the line.</p>\n<p>Intersection includes only the elements that are common to both drawings.</p>\n<p>For this intersection, only point B is in common.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\overline {AB}  \\cap \\overline {BC}  = B\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{\\overline {AB}}  \\cap {\\overline {BC}}  = B\">{\\overline {AB}}  \\cap {\\overline {BC}}  = B</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 532717,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BC}  \\cup \\overleftarrow {CA} \">\\overrightarrow {BC}  \\cup \\overleftarrow {CA} </span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You are looking for the union of ray <span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BC} \"></span> and the ray <span data-math=\"\\overleftarrow {CA} \"></span>.</p>\n<p>Be careful. They listed the points of the second ray looking backwards!</p>\n<p>Sketch the two rays separately above the line.</p>\n<p>Union includes all the elements that are in either drawing.</p>\n<p>For this union, the rays cover the entire line.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BC}  \\cup \\overleftarrow {CA}  = \\overleftrightarrow {AC}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BC}  \\cup \\overleftarrow {CA}  = \\overleftrightarrow {AC}\">\\overrightarrow {BC}  \\cup \\overleftarrow {CA}  = \\overleftrightarrow {AC}</span>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
